Year = {2013},
Volume = {6},
Number = {2},
Pages = {219-228},
Abstract = {The `Corona Verde' {[}Green Crown] Strategic Plan is a net of ecological
   corridors, greenways, rural areas and UNESCO sites, including all the
   open spaces in the metropolitan area of Turin (Italy). Its main goal is
   to link together policies for nature, landscape and cultural heritage,
   creating a new and alternative vision of the territory, based on the
   quality of the environment and of life. Since 2000, when the project
   started, more than epsilon 23 million have been invested by the European
   Union and the Piedmont Region, and, now, the first results can be
   analysed. Corona Verde introduces innovative approaches to environmental
   and urban strategies and in governance processes.},
